# BUG-279: the floor job of quality-gates.yml runs `node scripts/ci/check-workflows.mjs`
# with NO node_modules (every gate script there is zero-dependency on purpose).
# The first version of this fix imported js-yaml unconditionally and that job died with
# ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND (PR #285, run 42532246146) - so the gate now carries a
# zero-dependency rule (an unquoted plain scalar cannot contain ': ' - rule 4a) and
# parses with js-yaml wherever the module is installed (rule 4b). The script below is a
# byte-identical copy of scripts/ci/check-workflows.mjs placed in a directory with no
# node_modules anywhere above it, so the js-yaml import resolves to nothing.

$ node <copy with no node_modules> <pre-fix main-apk.yml fixture>
exit code: 1

check-workflows (BUG-067): 2 violation(s):
  main-apk.yml:113: a GitHub expression has no ?: operator - write it with && and || (BUG-279): ${{ steps.urls.outputs.configured == 'yes' ? 'pnpm' : '' }}
      cache: ${{ steps.urls.outputs.configured == 'yes' ? 'pnpm' : '' }}
  main-apk.yml:113: an unquoted plain scalar cannot contain ": " - GitHub's parser reads the whole file as invalid YAML and refuses the workflow before any job starts (BUG-279): quote the value, or use && and || for a conditional
      cache: ${{ steps.urls.outputs.configured == 'yes' ? 'pnpm' : '' }}

$ node <copy with no node_modules> <the fixed main-apk.yml>
exit code: 0

check-workflows: 1 workflows parse as YAML, carry only keys GitHub accepts, and read their inputs through the github context

$ node <copy with no node_modules> .github/workflows   (the whole tree, fixed)
exit code: 0

check-workflows: 16 workflows parse as YAML, carry only keys GitHub accepts, and read their inputs through the github context
